# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A table cell wears its own marker"

# TiddlyWiki reads a cell's leading marks before its content (core/…/rules/table.js):
# The bang builds a th rather than a td (:91), tilde sets rowspan (:35), the angle marks set
# and ^ and , set valign (:74). TiddlyWiki's own tiddlers carry 191 header rows.

|!Header A|!Header B|h
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 heading.th.meta.cell.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.cell.heading.th.tiddlywiki5
#          ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 heading.th.meta.cell.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.cell.heading.th.tiddlywiki5

|~|rowspan|
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 rowspan.down.meta.cell.td.tiddlywiki5 rowspan.down.punctuation.definition.cell.tiddlywiki5

|>|colspan right|
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 colspan.right.meta.cell.td.tiddlywiki5 colspan.right.punctuation.definition.cell.tiddlywiki5

# A left-colspan mark reads as table syntax, never as a stray angle bracket.
|<|colspan left|
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 colspan.left.meta.cell.td.tiddlywiki5 colspan.left.punctuation.definition.cell.tiddlywiki5
#^ - invalid.illegal.bad-angle-bracket.html.tiddlywiki5

|^top|,bottom|
#^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 meta.cell.valign.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.cell.valign.top.tiddlywiki5
#     ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 meta.cell.valign.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.cell.valign.bottom.tiddlywiki5

# Superscript and subscript keep their own reading at the head of a cell.
|^^sup^^ |,,sub,, |
#^ - punctuation.definition.cell.valign.top.tiddlywiki5

# An ordinary cell goes on carrying inline wikitext.
|a link |[[Some Target]] |
#          ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 markup.other.table.tiddlywiki5 markup.link.tiddlywiki5
